1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,431
Rub your closed eyes and you see sparkles and swirls — in total darkness.

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,197
They have a name: phosphenes — seeing light when no light enters the eye.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:14,057
At the back of your eye, the retina has cells that react to light.

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:19,697
Pressing on the eyeball squeezes those cells, so they fire signals anyway.

5
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:25,133
The signal travels up the optic nerve, and your brain reads it as light.

6
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,867
Similar sparkles can pop up when you stand up fast or after a big sneeze.

7
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:32,577
So rub gently.

8
00:00:32,577 --> 00:00:35,355
Pressing hard on your eyes isn't good for them.

9
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:39,949
Flashes on their own, new floaters or a shadow over your vision?

10
00:00:39,949 --> 00:00:41,221
See a doctor urgently.
